  ($q$turkey-burgers$q$, 3, $q$Fry in a pan on medium heat or grill until internal temperature reaches 165 °F.$q$, $q$Fry in a skillet on medium heat or grill until internal temperature reaches 165 °F.$q$),
  ($q$turkey-stew$q$, 2, $q$Add potatoes, tomatoes, and water to pan. Bring to a boil, then lower heat and simmer 30 minutes or until vegetables are tender. Add turkey and cook another five minutes or until heated.$q$, $q$Add potatoes, tomatoes, and water to saucepan. Bring to a boil, then lower heat and simmer 30 minutes or until vegetables are tender. Add turkey and cook another five minutes or until heated.$q$),
  ($q$vegetable-cheese-soup$q$, 1, $q$Bring 2 cups water to a boil. Add vegetables, onions, salt, and curry powder, if using. Reduce heat, cover and cook until almost tender.$q$, $q$Bring 2 cups water to a boil in a pot. Add vegetables, onions, salt, and curry powder, if using. Reduce heat, cover and cook until almost tender.$q$),
  ($q$vegetable-tacos$q$, 1, $q$Sauté onion, garlic and jalapeno, add cumin, salt, and black pepper. When everything is soft, add red pepper and mushrooms. Sauté for 2 more minutes.$q$, $q$In a skillet, sauté onion, garlic and jalapeno, add cumin, salt, and black pepper. When everything is soft, add red pepper and mushrooms. Sauté for 2 more minutes.$q$),
  ($q$veggie-burgers$q$, 5, $q$In a large pan, brown both sides of the patties over medium to high heat for 5 to 8 minutes.$q$, $q$In a large skillet, brown both sides of the patties over medium to high heat for 5 to 8 minutes.$q$),
  ($q$veggie-chow-mein$q$, 1, $q$Prepare noodles according to package directions. Drain and set aside.$q$, $q$Prepare noodles in a pot according to package directions. Drain and set aside.$q$),
  ($q$veggie-quesadillas$q$, 2, $q$Spray pan with cooking oil spray.$q$, $q$Spray skillet with cooking oil spray.$q$),
  ($q$veggie-quesadillas$q$, 3, $q$Cook vegetables on medium heat for 4 to 5 minutes, stirring frequently. Remove from pan.$q$, $q$Cook vegetables on medium heat for 4 to 5 minutes, stirring frequently. Remove from skillet.$q$),
  ($q$veggie-quesadillas$q$, 4, $q$Spray pan with cooking spray. Place tortilla in the pan. Sprinkle with half the vegetables and half of the cheese.$q$, $q$Spray skillet with cooking spray. Place tortilla in the skillet. Sprinkle with half the vegetables and half of the cheese.$q$),
  ($q$white-chili$q$, 1, $q$Sauté peppers and onion in oil.$q$, $q$Sauté peppers and onion in oil in a pot.$q$),
  ($q$whole-wheat-garlic-bread-sticks$q$, 5, $q$Bake in preheated oven for about 25 minutes or until crisp and lightly browned.$q$, $q$Bake on a sheet pan in preheated oven for about 25 minutes or until crisp and lightly browned.$q$),
  ($q$zingy-lemon-chicken-pasta$q$, 3, $q$Prepare pasta according to package directions and drain. Combine sauce, chicken, and pasta mixture.$q$, $q$Prepare pasta in a pot according to package directions and drain. Combine sauce, chicken, and pasta mixture.$q$),
  ($q$zucchini-and-tomatoes$q$, 5, $q$Cover pan, reduce heat, and cook until vegetables are tender.$q$, $q$Cover saucepan, reduce heat, and cook until vegetables are tender.$q$),
